6559,"d":1320,"wp":"en:NTNU University Museum","wd":"Q1770886","ds":"The NTNU University Museum (Norwegian: Vitenskapsmuseet) in Trondheim is one of seven Norwegian university museums with natural and cultural history collections and exhibits. The museum has research and administrative responsibility over archaeology and biology in Central Norway. Additionally, the museum operates comprehensive community outreach programs and has exhibits in wooden buildings in Kalvskinnet.","wpu":"NTNU University Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/DKNVS-museet_Trondheim.jpg/960px-DKNVS-museet_Trondheim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Comfort Hotel Park","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":63.427648,"lo":10.392482,"d":1331,"w":"https://www.nordicchoicehotels.com/hotels/norway/trondheim/comfort-hotel-park/","ph":"+47 73 83 39 00","f":["wc"],"wifi":1},{"n":"Trondheim Kunstmuseum Bispegata","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":63.427356,"lo":10.394517,"d":1334,"h":"Tu-Fr 11:00-18:00; Sa, Su 11:00-16:00","w":"https://trondheimkunstmuseum.no/","wp":"en:Trondheim Art Museum","wd":"Q12007630","ds":"The Trondheim Art Museum (Norwegian: Trondheim Kunstmuseum, previously Trøndelag Kunstgalleri) is an art museum located in Trondheim in Sør-Trøndelag county, Norway. The museum shows temporary exhibitions of international and regional art in dialogue with works from the museum's collection. The museum possesses Norway's third largest public art collection with an emphasis on art since 1850.","wpu":"Trondheim Art Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Trondheim_Kunstnuseum%2C_Innherredsveien_20.jpg/960px-Trondheim_Kunstnuseum%2C_Innherredsveien_20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Trondhjems Kunstforening","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":63.427403,"lo":10.393626,"d":1340,"w":"https://tkf.no","f":["free"]},{"n":"Nidaros Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":63.426918,"lo":10.396904,"d":1358,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00; Sa 09:00-14:00; Su 13:00-17:00","w":"http://Nidarosdomen.no","ph":"+47 73 89 08 00","wp":"en:Nidaros Cathedral","wd":"Q215023","ds":"Nidaros Cathedral (Norwegian: Nidarosdomen / Nidaros domkirke) is a Church of Norway cathedral located in the city of Trondheim in Trøndelag county. It is built over the burial site of King Olav II (c. 995–1030, reigned 1015–1028), who brought Christianity to Norway and became the patron saint of the nation; the consecration of new Norwegian monarchs occurs at Nidaros Cathedral.","wpu":"Nidaros Cathedral","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Nidaros_Cathedral%2C_Trondheim%2C_West_view_20150605_1.jpg/960px-Nidaros_Cathedral%2C_Trondheim%2C_West_view_20150605_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Akron Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":63.426686,"lo":10.403626,"d":1375,"w":"https://www.akrongallery.com/"},{"n":"Norsk Døvemuseum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":63.42732,"lo":10.391401,"d":1383,"h":"Th-Fr 11:00-15:00; Sa 12:00-16:00","w":"https://norsk-dovemuseum.no/","wp":"en:Norsk Døvemuseum","wd":"Q7053425","ds":"Norsk Døvemuseum ('Norwegian Deaf Museum') is a museum in Trondheim, Norway. It is a division of Trøndelag Folkemuseum. The museum is located in Rødbygget, which was drawn by Christian Heinrich Grosch.","wpu":"Norsk Døvemuseum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/D%C3%B8vehistorisk_museum_Trondheim_01.jpg/960px-D%C3%B8vehistorisk_museum_Trondheim_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Middelalderutstilling","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":63.428355,"lo":10.386085,"d":1396},{"n":"BABEL","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":63.437974,"lo":10.42917,"d":1405,"w":"https://www.babelkunst.no/"},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":63.44015,"lo":10.399445,"d":149},{"n":"Rema 1000 Pirsenteret","g":"essentials","k":"supe