ke Bank","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":63.432097,"lo":10.400829,"d":767,"h":"Mo-Th 08:00-21:00; Fr 08:00-18:00; Sa 10:00-15:00; Su 15:00-20:00","ph":"+47 98708540"},{"n":"Vitusapotek Solsiden","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":63.434383,"lo":10.413105,"d":791,"h":"Mo-Sa 08:30-24:00, Su 10:00-24:00","ph":"+47 73883737","f":["wc"]},{"n":"Verftsbrua","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.435278,"lo":10.4075,"d":525,"ds":"Verftsbrua (Norwegian for \"Yard Bridge\"), also popularly called Blomsterbrua (\"Flower Bridge\"), is a bridge at the bay of Trondheim. The bridge, built in 2003, spans 125 metres (410 ft). The name Verftsbrua comes from the nearby shipyard, Trondhjems mekaniske Værksted, while the name Blomsterbrua is due to the bridge featuring flowerbeds along its edges.","wpu":"Verftsbrua","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Verftsbrua_Fra_Bakkebru.jpg/960px-Verftsbrua_Fra_Bakkebru.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bakke Church (Trondheim)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.43282,"lo":10.410502,"d":833,"ds":"Bakke Church (Norwegian: Bakke kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Trondheim Municipality in Trøndelag county, Norway. It is located in the Bakklandet area of the city of Trondheim, and the church serves the Bakklandet, Møllenberg, Rosenborg, and Nedre Elvehavn areas of Østbyen in Trondheim.","wpu":"Bakke Church (Trondheim)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/Bakke_kirke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Olav Tryggvason (statue)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.430556,"lo":10.395,"d":985,"ds":"A statue of Olav Tryggvason is located in Trondheim, Norway. Sculpted by sculptor Wilhelm Rasmussen, it honors King Olav Tryggvason, who was the city's founder. The 18-metre (58-foot) high statue is mounted on top of an obelisk.","wpu":"Olav Tryggvason (statue)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Trondheim_-_monument_01.jpg/960px-Trondheim_-_monument_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vår Frue Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.430169,"lo":10.398162,"d":992,"ds":"Vår Frue Church (Norwegian: Vår Frue kirke / English: Our Lady's Church) is a medieval parish church of the Church of Norway in Trondheim Municipality in Trøndelag county, Norway. It is located in the downtown Midtbyen area of the city of Trondheim, just a few blocks north of the Nidaros Cathedral.","wpu":"Vår Frue Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Trondheim_-_V%C3%A5r_Frue_church.jpg/960px-Trondheim_-_V%C3%A5r_Frue_church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Trøndelag Teater","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.4292,"lo":10.3917,"d":1183,"ds":"Trøndelag Teater is a large theater in the city of Trondheim, in Trøndelag county, Norway. Trøndelag Teater stages large-scale dance and musical performances.","wpu":"Trøndelag Teater","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Trondelag_Teater.JPG/960px-Trondelag_Teater.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kristiansten Fortress","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.426944,"lo":10.410556,"d":1422,"ds":"Kristiansten Fortress (Norwegian: Kristiansten Festning, historically spelled Christiansten) is located on a hill east of the city of Trondheim which is located within Trondheim Municipality in Trøndelag county, Norway, named after Christian V of Denmark-Norway. It was built after the city fire of Trondheim in 1681 to protect the city against attack from the east. Construction was finished in 1685.","wpu":"Kristiansten Fortress","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Kristiansten_Fortress_Trondheim_2009_1.JPG/960px-Kristiansten_Fortress_Trondheim_2009_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lademoen Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.437078,"lo":10.430328,"d":1473,"ds":"Lademoen Church (Norwegian: Lademoen kirke) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Trondheim Municipality in Trøndelag county, Norway. It is located in the Lademoen area of the city of Trondheim, immediately north of the old European route E6 highway. It is one of the churches for the Bakklandet og Lademoen parish which is part of the Nidaros domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Nidaros.","wpu":"Lademoen Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Lademoen_Church_Trondheim_2009_1.JPG/960px-Lademoen_Church_Trondheim_2009_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Norwegian National Museum of Justice","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":63.4303,"lo":10.3781,"d":1494,"ds":"The Norwegian National Museum of Justice (Norwegian: Justismuseet, until 2016 Norsk Rettsmuseum) is a public museum of penal justice and law enforcement in Trondheim, Norway. It is housed in a former prison. From 2001-2017, the director of the museum was Johan Sigfred Helberg.","wpu":"Norwegian National Museum of Justice","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/The_National_Museum_of_Justice_Norway.jpg/960px-The_National_Museum_of_Justice_Norway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Trondheim ( TRON(D)-hyme; Urban East Norwegian: [ˈtrɔ̂nː(h)æɪm]; Southern Sami: Tråante), historically Kaupangen, Nidaros, and Trondhjem (locally [ˈtrɔ̂nːjæm] ), is a city and municipality in Trøndelag county, Norway. As of 1 January 2026, it had a population of 218,460. Trondheim is the third most populous municipality in Norway, and is the fourth largest urban area.","wpu":"Trondheim","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Trondheim_overview_01.jpg/960px-Trondheim_overview_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}